  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xf6" flags="0x0">
    <title>B2 - Supercharger upper pressure ratio diagnosis threshold</title>
    <description>Maximum modeled supercharger pressure ratio versus engine speed. A sustained excess confirmed by diagnosis selects the bypass fallback position. Evidence: CPU CB406..CB444: interpolate pointer834F (DPP2=23 -&gt; fileC34F), compare E2D6 &gt; (lookup &lt;&lt;8), qualify through D30D0 and latch FD30.6. CB4A0..CB4A4 combines FD30.5/6 into FD30.4; E32FA..E3330 selects fallback cal971E. Confidence: confirmed_code Source image: C230Kompressor_SIM4LE_5WK90416_M10062_6577815126_full.bin. Calibration block 2. Monitor enabled with FD12.8 set and FD2A.5, FD52.9, FD30.4 and FD22.12 clear. Ratio = raw/64, not bar or gauge boost. The upper monitor uses modeled E2D6, approximately 16384*E2BE/E2C8, rather than direct measured MAP/ambient pressure. Diagnostic qualification time in seconds, complete latch-reset conditions and exact DTC mapping are not established.</description>
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x0" mmedaddress="0x11103" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedcolcount="8" mmedmajorstridebits="8" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
