    <title>B5 - Bypass actuator integral increment curve</title>
    <description>Increment added to motor integral state, then clamped by9A94/9A96. Evidence: CPU E27DC..E2888 selects axis and curve using BC002/BC1F2, subtracts0x8000; sums terms. E288C..E2928 limits and outputs PW3. Confidence: confirmed_code Source image: C230Kompressor_SIM4LE_5WK90416_M10062_6577815126_full.bin. Calibration block 5. Second motorized air flap: actual E3A2, target E3C4, motor PW3; distinct from main throttle E5EA/PW2. Bypass/recirculation identification is strongly supported by the air-path calculation and two-actuator architecture, but no verified physical connector-to-RAM or manufacturer symbol has been recovered. Position values remain native sensor counts, not degrees or percent. Actuator-control calibration, not a requested boost or flap-position map. Motor command units are native, centered raw32768.</description>
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x2" mmedaddress="0x2695a" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedcolcount="8" mmedmajorstridebits="16" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
